    <p class="paraHeader">THE PROBLEM WITH TODAY’S EDUCATION</p>  
    <p class="paraCommon">For most of modern history, schooling followed the needs of factories, long hours, fixed schedules, batch processing, standardized outputs. </p>
    <p class="paraCommon">Students were expected to sit still, memorize, reproduce. </p>
    <p class="paraCommon"><b>But the world flipped. Work flipped. Technology flipped. </b></p>
    <p class="paraCommon">Only our education system forgot to flip.</p>  
     <p class="paraCommon">Today:
         <ul>
             
               <li>Students spend <b>15 years studying,</b> but step into real work feeling confused.</li>
               <li>Employers keep saying <b>“graduates are not job-ready.”</b></li>
               <li>Students chase degrees, but hide the fact that they secretly learned more from YouTube, Random Projects, and their Own Curiosity.</li>
               <li>Families invest lakhs in coaching and marks, but the actual learning happens when a student finally enters a real workplace.</li>
         </ul>

</p>
    <p class="paraCommon">And yet internships continue to be treated as a <b>“short summer activity”</b> instead of the <b>core engine of modern learning.</b> </p>  
     <p class="paraCommon">This is the gap we are fixing.</p>
